            "end_line": 23,
            "line_count": 3,
            "preview": "// Template mixes a normal reference \"${not-escaped}\" with an escaped one \"$${escaped}\". // The escape character is '$', so the leading \"$$\" escapes the following \"${escaped}\". final String template = \"${not-escaped} $${escaped}\";"
          },
          {
            "start_line": 25,
            "end_line": 26,
            "line_count": 2,
            "preview": "final Map<String, String> variables = new HashMap<>(); variables.put(\"not-escaped\", \"value\");"
          },
          {
            "start_line": 28,
            "end_line": 29,
            "line_count": 2,
            "preview": "// Substitutor using \"${\" / \"}\" delimiters and '$' as the escape character. final StrSubstitutor sub = new StrSubstitutor(variables, \"${\", \"}\", '$');"
          },
          {
            "start_line": 31,
            "end_line": 34,
            "line_count": 4,
            "preview": "// By default escapes are NOT preserved: the escape character is consumed, // leaving the literal \"${escaped}\" in the output. assertFalse(sub.isPreserveEscapes());"
          },
          {
            "start_line": 36,
            "end_line": 40,
            "line_count": 5,
            "preview": "// With escape preservation enabled the escape character is kept, // so the output still contains the original \"$${escaped}\". sub.setPreserveEscapes(true);"
          }
